SUMMARY
------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------------
The CommandConfirmDialog surface itself is COMPLETE and INDEPENDENTLY VERIFIED GREEN on iOS + macOS
(build + 42 XCTests per platform, swiftlint --strict, swiftformat --lint, check-placeholders all clean).

The whole-app acceptance gate (`xcodebuild -scheme TeslaSync ... build test`) is BLOCKED by PRE-EXISTING,
OUT-OF-SCOPE breakage that exists at HEAD independently of this surface:
  • iOS: duplicate public top-level types `RecentDrives*` and `StateTimeline*` are each defined TWICE —
    in TeslaSync/dashboard-widgets (RecentDrivesListWidget.*, StateTimelineWidget.*) AND in
    TeslaSync/feature-views (RecentDrivesSection.*, StateTimeline.*). Swift reports "ambiguous for type
    lookup". These 4 sibling surfaces are owned by other P4 prompts; per the allowed-files list this
    prompt may touch ONLY apps/apple/TeslaSync/modals-dialogs/CommandConfirmDialog.* + this log.
  • macOS: additionally blocked by code-signing entitlements (TeslaSync-macOS / TeslaSyncWidgets-macOS
    "require signing with a development certificate") — a runner/platform-capability limitation, plus the
    same duplicate-type collisions underneath.

PROOF the block is pre-existing and NOT caused by this surface: regenerating the project at HEAD config
(CommandConfirmDialog NOT referenced — `grep -c CommandConfirmDialog project.pbxproj` = 0) and building
the full app FAILS identically (see BASELINE sections). CommandConfirmDialog uses only `CommandConfirm*`
-prefixed types and references no `RecentDrives*`/`StateTimeline*` symbol.

